<p>The U.S. Treasury Department announced sanctions on Friday against 10 individuals and companies it accused of helping Iran’s military obtain weapons and raw materials used in Shahed drones and ballistic missiles. The targets include entities in China and Hong Kong, as well as individuals and companies based in Belarus and the United Arab Emirates. The Treasury said it remained ready to take further economic action against Iran’s military-industrial base to prevent Tehran from rebuilding production capacity or projecting power outside its borders. The measures were announced days before President Trump is scheduled to travel to China for talks with President Xi Jinping, and as efforts to end the war with Iran have stalled. The sanctions add the listed parties to the U.S. Treasury’s restricted list, freezing any U.S.-linked assets and generally barring U.S. persons from doing business with them.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/A2laq4zwMDnzEWQy8WmXglH9mVk115i0qO0QRnVuHGQ4TZkHwoqrPheZrTTvC0KAvE9ZAj3B_oeRDKzxympfkCPOF6Ks2d3DacwYcqT9LPMtlENOuMSfmWbZbG8hQRdYkHQP8GVB_VN0Mb6xXcoKF7b0cIiLLg5JI-g_hzQ8WKZ9P71uD-HtSGumjscvtl29alHuL1BTmVeKhhKUp9qGW8za8-SGUPPwc6e6FNO-UTlyzE-lHq2za8sL1AGD5SgP_UxP48RmI4ez' alt='Image accompanying coverage of U.S. sanctions targeting Iran-linked weapons procurement networks.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Oil pressure: The Treasury warned it could impose secondary sanctions on international financial institutions that help Iran, including those tied to China’s independent “teapot” oil refineries.</li><li>Drone capacity: The British government-backed Centre for Information Resilience has assessed that Iran can manufacture nearly 10,000 drones a month.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Scott Bessent, U.S. Treasury secretary: Bessent said Washington would keep pursuing foreign individuals and companies that supply Iran’s military with weapons for use against U.S. forces. (<a href='https://www.pravda.com.ua/news/2026/05/09/8033910/'>Ukrainska Pravda</a>)</li><li>Brett Erickson, managing principal at Obsidian Risk Advisors: Erickson said the sanctions were intended to curb Iran’s ability to threaten commercial shipping in the Strait of Hormuz and challenge regional allies. (<a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/u-s-sanctions-firms-accused-of-supporting-irans-weapons-programme-552728/'>Minute Mirror</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/us-imposes-sanctions-on-10-individuals-companies-for-aiding-irans-weapons-sector'>US imposes sanctions on companies it accuses of aiding Iran’s weapons sector</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/us-imposes-sanctions-10-individuals-companies-aiding-irans-weapons-sector'>US imposes sanctions on 10 individuals, companies for aiding Iran&#x27;s weapons sector</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-imposes-sanctions-on-10-individuals-companies-for-aiding-irans-weapons-sector/article70957188.ece'>U.S. imposes sanctions on 10 individuals, companies for aiding Iran’s weapons sector</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='http://www.adaderana.lk/news.php?nid=122269'>US imposes sanctions on companies it accuses of aiding Iran s weapons sector</a> - adaderana.lk</li><li><a href='https://indianexpress.com/article/world/us-news/iran-war-live-tehrans-reply-to-us-deal-expected-amid-clashes-in-hormuz-10680435/'>Iran-US War Live Updates: US imposes sanctions on companies it accuses of aiding Iran’s weapons sector</a> - indianexpress.com</li><li><a href='https://dailytimes.com.pk/1490976/us-sanctions-entities-over-alleged-support-to-iran-arms-efforts/'>US sanctions entities over alleged support to Iran arms efforts</a> - dailytimes.com.pk</li><li><a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/u-s-sanctions-firms-accused-of-supporting-irans-weapons-programme-552728/'>U.S. sanctions firms accused of supporting Iran’...</a> - minutemirror.com.pk</li><li><a href=